{
  "assessment": "Independent source-closure review passes this matched family. Frozen arXiv 2502.06256v3 lines 78-85 and 144-154 derive the self-similar exponent beta=1/(k+2); lines 85, 95-105, and 111 support the two-dimensional high-Peclet k=3 experiment and R(t) proportional to t^(1/5), while lines 86, 108, 117, 123, 154, and 158 support the deterministic two-dimensional k=1 simulation and R(t) proportional to t^(1/3). Within one branch and one source-defined self-similar regime, dividing R(t)=A t^beta by R(t_ref)=A t_ref^beta gives the authored amplitude-free truth Y=R(t)/R(t_ref)=q^beta exactly; no unreported amplitude is set and [1,10] is explicitly only a conservative positive benchmark query interval. The compiled Oracle has exactly one expression tree, y=power(q,beta_k3). Its only referenced parameter is beta_k3: the historical map binds that shared slot to the source beta_k3=0.2, and the counterfactual map binds it to the source beta_k1=1/3. This canonical shared-slot compilation contains no k/world selector and no inactive parameter. Independent execution at 100,001 evenly spaced q values per branch was finite, strictly increasing, and matched q^(1/5) and q^(1/3) with zero floating-point discrepancy; endpoints were [1,1.5848931924611136] and [1,2.154434690031884]. All four stored diagnostic/hidden predictions matched exactly, and repeated Oracle calls at five conditions per branch were bit-identical and equal to the authoritative formula. Historical and counterfactual CaseDefinitions were identical after removing their opaque instance IDs in both tracks. The actual Discovery definition contains no exponent, numerical branch value, power-law formula, or candidate-family scaffold: it exposes only the source-supported apparatus, normalized variables, branch-neutral two-dimensional overdamped conditions, and qualitative self-similar profile-collapse regime; the exact expression template appears only in Identification as intended. The k=3 experimental and k=1 simulation conditions remain Oracle-private. Known-truth submissions passed historical/Identification, historical/Discovery, counterfactual/Identification, and counterfactual/Discovery with zero hidden-test scaled error. The deterministic central-relation readout and provenance-only source-uncertainty wording are accurate. No unresolved source-fidelity, Oracle, public/private-boundary, prediction, direction, determinism, or four-cell viability issue remains.",
